course: dictionary
lesson: 5461
title: Glowing fish of the deep sea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lanternfish is a small fish that lives deep in the ocean, far below where sunlight reaches. Its name is a clue: the spots on its body glow with light, like tiny lanterns.
explain: Context helps with new words. «Lanternfish have light organs called photophores along their bodies» tells you the light comes from special organs in the skin, not from a torch or the sun.
explain: «They are among the most common fish on Earth» means there are very many of them. Read the whole sentence to find the meaning, then check it by swapping in your own words.
fact: A lanternfish is a small deep-sea fish with spots on its body that glow with light.
fact: «Photophores» are light organs, the parts that make the glowing light on a lanternfish.
fact: Lanternfish are among the most common fish in the world.
fact: At night lanternfish swim up near the surface to feed, and in the day they go deep down.
fact: Only the tiny bristlemouths may be more numerous than lanternfish.
exercise: «Lanternfish have light organs called photophores along their bodies.» What are photophores? | *Light organs that give out light | Holes in the sea floor | Fins used for swimming | Tiny teeth in the mouth
exercise: When do lanternfish swim up near the surface to feed? | *At night | Never, they stay on the sea floor | In the day | At the start of winter
exercise: «Lanternfish are among the most common fish on Earth.» What does common mean here? | Very rare and hard to find | Rude or badly behaved | *Found in large numbers | Shiny and bright like a lantern
test: Where do lanternfish go during the day? | Up to the surface where it is sunny | *Deep down in the ocean | Onto the beach | Into rivers and lakes
test: Which animal may be more numerous than lanternfish? | *Bristlemouths | Whales | Elephants | Sharks
exam: What does lanternfish mean? | A ship that carries lights at night | *A small deep-sea fish with glowing spots on its body | A plant that grows on the sea floor | A large shark with bright white teeth
